@philwo Thank you for the details explanation. I haven only one question: What changed, why it is starting to fail now, or was `bazel clean` always broken?

> David, why are you running clean in the first place?

This is an absolute exception here, I was doing this while updating bazlets. In Gitiles or Gerrit we are using bazlets, with `git_repository`. Now, while working with bazlets code, I found, that only changing the bazlets source wouldn't re-fetch the bazlets. That why I used `bazel clean` and have discovered this issue.
